# The EMPTY BRANCH form, which is R24's own oracle-split family: python and
# libpcre2 agree on every span and can differ on group 1 (python reports an
# empty span at the loop's end where libpcre2 reports the last iteration
# that consumed). §3.6's rule is INVESTIGATE, not filter -- the span is kept
# because both authorities assert it, and a slot-only divergence is dropped
# with a note rather than pinned to whichever oracle was asked first.
pattern (|a){0,12}b
n ""
n "a"
m "b" 0 1
g 1 0 0
n "c"
n "ac"
m "bc" 0 1
g 1 0 0
m "abc" 0 2
# ^ SPAN ONLY: the two oracles disagree on this
#   cell's group 1 (python ((1, 1),), libpcre2 ((0, 1),)) and
#   this is the `(|a){m,n}` family [R24 S-F5]
#   measured as the one where they do. pcrec agreed
#   with libpcre2 on all 15,600 cells of that sweep,
#   so the slot is not pinned here rather than pinned
#   to whichever oracle was asked first.
n "aac"
m "abac" 0 2
# ^ SPAN ONLY: the two oracles disagree on this
#   cell's group 1 (python ((1, 1),), libpcre2 ((0, 1),)) and
#   this is the `(|a){m,n}` family [R24 S-F5]
#   measured as the one where they do. pcrec agreed
#   with libpcre2 on all 15,600 cells of that sweep,
#   so the slot is not pinned here rather than pinned
#   to whichever oracle was asked first.
m "aabc" 0 3
# ^ SPAN ONLY: the two oracles disagree on this
#   cell's group 1 (python ((2, 2),), libpcre2 ((1, 2),)) and
#   this is the `(|a){m,n}` family [R24 S-F5]
#   measured as the one where they do. pcrec agreed
#   with libpcre2 on all 15,600 cells of that sweep,
#   so the slot is not pinned here rather than pinned
#   to whichever oracle was asked first.
n "aaac"
n "aaaac"
n "aaaaac"
n "aaaaaaaac"
n "aaaaaaaaac"
n "aaaaaaaaaac"
m "ababababc" 0 2
# ^ SPAN ONLY: the two oracles disagree on this
#   cell's group 1 (python ((1, 1),), libpcre2 ((0, 1),)) and
#   this is the `(|a){m,n}` family [R24 S-F5]
#   measured as the one where they do. pcrec agreed
#   with libpcre2 on all 15,600 cells of that sweep,
#   so the slot is not pinned here rather than pinned
#   to whichever oracle was asked first.
m "abababababc" 0 2
# ^ SPAN ONLY: the two oracles disagree on this
#   cell's group 1 (python ((1, 1),), libpcre2 ((0, 1),)) and
#   this is the `(|a){m,n}` family [R24 S-F5]
#   measured as the one where they do. pcrec agreed
#   with libpcre2 on all 15,600 cells of that sweep,
#   so the slot is not pinned here rather than pinned
#   to whichever oracle was asked first.
m "aabbc" 0 3
# ^ SPAN ONLY: the two oracles disagree on this
#   cell's group 1 (python ((2, 2),), libpcre2 ((1, 2),)) and
#   this is the `(|a){m,n}` family [R24 S-F5]
#   measured as the one where they do. pcrec agreed
#   with libpcre2 on all 15,600 cells of that sweep,
#   so the slot is not pinned here rather than pinned
#   to whichever oracle was asked first.
m "abbc" 0 2
# ^ SPAN ONLY: the two oracles disagree on this
#   cell's group 1 (python ((1, 1),), libpcre2 ((0, 1),)) and
#   this is the `(|a){m,n}` family [R24 S-F5]
#   measured as the one where they do. pcrec agreed
#   with libpcre2 on all 15,600 cells of that sweep,
#   so the slot is not pinned here rather than pinned
#   to whichever oracle was asked first.
m "baac" 0 1
g 1 0 0
n "aaaaaaaaaaaac"
n "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaac"
m "ababababababababc" 0 2
# ^ SPAN ONLY: the two oracles disagree on this
#   cell's group 1 (python ((1, 1),), libpcre2 ((0, 1),)) and
#   this is the `(|a){m,n}` family [R24 S-F5]
#   measured as the one where they do. pcrec agreed
#   with libpcre2 on all 15,600 cells of that sweep,
#   so the slot is not pinned here rather than pinned
#   to whichever oracle was asked first.
n "q"
n "aq"
m "abq" 0 2
# ^ SPAN ONLY: the two oracles disagree on this
#   cell's group 1 (python ((1, 1),), libpcre2 ((0, 1),)) and
#   this is the `(|a){m,n}` family [R24 S-F5]
#   measured as the one where they do. pcrec agreed
#   with libpcre2 on all 15,600 cells of that sweep,
#   so the slot is not pinned here rather than pinned
