# ratio moves for reasons OTHER than an alternation lowering, or the bar goes
# on being re-pinned every time an emitter axis reshapes its witnesses --
# which is exactly what [ENG-ISL] did to the old fixed pair. This one is
# CLASS-LEADING (`[ab]a|[ab]`), so the VM's alternation island declines it by
# construction and [OPT-CLSPACK]'s class work is what would move it instead.
# Expectations from python3 `re`, which supports possessive quantifiers.
pattern (?:[ab]a|[ab]){8,12}+b
m "abbbbbbbbbbbb" 0 13
m "bbbbbbbbbbbbb" 0 13
m "aaabbbbbbbbbbb" 0 14
m "abaabbbbbbbbbb" 0 14
n ""
n "b"
n "ab"
n "aaaaaaaab"
n "babababababab"
n "aaaaaaaaaaaaab"

# [ART-SIZE] §9 witness-pool member — island-bearing (four prefix-free literals), ladder TAKEN.
# The pool must be CORPUS patterns (run_size_term.sh §9's own comment says
# why); expectations from python3 `re`.
pattern (?:ab|ba|aa|bb){24}c
m "ababababababababababababababababababababababababc" 0 49
m "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaac" 0 49
m "abbaabbaabbaabbaabbaabbaabbaabbaabbaabbaabbaabbac" 0 49
n ""
n "z"
n "abz"

# [ART-SIZE] §9 witness-pool member — island-bearing prefix ladder, four alternatives.
# The pool must be CORPUS patterns (run_size_term.sh §9's own comment says
# why); expectations from python3 `re`.
pattern (?:abcd|abc|ab|a){17}z
m "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaz" 0 18
m "abcdabcdabcdabcdabcdabcdabcdabcdabcdabcdabcdabcdabcdabcdabcdabcdabcdz" 0 69
m "abababababababababababababababababz" 0 35
n ""
n "z"
n "abz"

# [ART-SIZE] §9 witness-pool member — class-leading, ladder DECLINED.
# The pool must be CORPUS patterns (run_size_term.sh §9's own comment says
# why); expectations from python3 `re`.
pattern (?:[ab]a|[ab]){9,12}+b
m "abbbbbbbbbbbb" 0 13
m "bbbbbbbbbbbbb" 0 13
m "aaabbbbbbbbbbb" 0 14
n ""
n "z"
n "abz"

# [ART-SIZE] §9 witness-pool member — prefix-bearing width 2 (the island's knee declines it).
# The pool must be CORPUS patterns (run_size_term.sh §9's own comment says
# why); expectations from python3 `re`.
pattern (?:ab|a){8,12}+b
m "aaaaaaaabb" 0 10
m "aaaaaaaaabb" 0 11
m "aaaaaaaabba" 0 10
n ""
n "z"
n "abz"

# [ART-SIZE] §9 witness-pool member, and the pool's second ISLAND-STAMPING one.
# The first was a prefix LADDER, which the island's size rule now declines (a
# ladder's try sites grow quadratically in its depth) — the pool check caught
# that loss itself, which is what its island-coverage floor is for. This one
# is a four-word set with one prefix relation, so it stamps an island AND
# reaches the unroll ladder.
pattern (?:cat|cats|dog|dogs){12}z
m "catcatcatcatcatcatcatcatcatcatcatcatz" 0 37
m "catscatscatscatscatscatscatscatscatscatscatscatsz" 0 49
m "dogdogdogdogdogdogdogdogdogdogdogdogz" 0 37
m "catdogcatdogcatdogcatdogcatdogcatdogz" 0 37
n ""
n "catz"
n "z"
